GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `add one` n IS n + 1

-- Unknown annotations on either side of a known one, and one after a rule.
@future-annotation an annotation a newer version might define
@desc the second rule adds two
@future-annotation and another one, directly above the rule
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `add two` n IS n + 2
@trailing-future-annotation

#ASSERT (`add one` 1) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT (`add two` 1) EQUALS 3
